Mechanism:
    Request & response like http
    no pipelining is supported
    authentication is supported, need to learn
    tls is supported, need to learn, probably nothing much needed, should already have a well known library
    must be connection oriented since auth is planned i.e server must be aware of state attached to the connection
    timeout: needed?

Syntax structure of request:
    design questions:
        what should be the symbols for {start},{end}, {separator}?
            Instead of relying on start and end, i've decided to go with a 4-byte payload length and then message payload. This will reduce need for separate, start and end
            markers.
        Should we include length of each param before?
            pros: once a size int is read, we can know exactly how many bytes to read from connection to get the value. Now we have to check for each n series of characters
                read to see if it is a separator.
            cons: message length is increased.
        Should i do text based protocol like resp used by redis or custom binary protocol.
        Binary protocol seems to be interesting let's do that.
    {Start}{Command}{seperator}{Key}{seperator}{dataType}{Seperator}{Value}{seperator}{ttl}{seperator}{end}

    {Start}: required
    {Command}: required. Supported values {SET, GET, EXISTS, DELE}
    {seperator}: required
    {Key}: required
    {seperator}: required
    {Value}: optional
    {seperator}: optional
    {ttl}: optional, should be non negative epoch value
    {seperator}: optional
    {dataType}: optional, Supported types { stringType, integerType, longType, boolType, characterType}
    {Seperator}: optional
    {end}: required

    Custom binary format:
    {4bytes} : length of the entire message, required
    {1byte}: command, 255 commands are a lot, so one byte would do, required
    {2bytes}: length of key, 65536 characters are enough for key, required
    {n bytes}: n bytes as mentioned by previous value, required
    {1byte}: data type of value if value is present, optional for get, exists, delete
    {4bytes}: length of the data, 2^32-1 is big enough for value
    {n bytes}: n bytes as mentioned by previous value
    {8 bytes}: ttl required always, if not present error out

    Length of message comes up to: 1 + 2 + 2 + 4 + 8 + x + y = 17 + x + y; max if x is 2^16-1 and max of y is 2^32 -1, so clearly i need min of 2^64-1 number. That is
    i need 8 bytes to indicate the length of the message.
    but 2^32-1, is 4GB of payload that is too much, i think 1MB value and 65kkb key i.e 2MB for the command is max enough. so 2*2^20 ~ 21 bits are needed for specifying the
    payload length.

Syntax structure of response:
    {Start}{OperationResponseCode}{separator}{Key}{seperator}{dataType}{Seperator}{Value}{seperator}{end}

    {Start}: required
    {OperationResponseCode}: required. Valid values {EXISTS, NOTEXISTS, CREATED,FOUND,FAILED,DELETED,INVALID_OPERATION}
    {seperator}: required
    {Key}: required
    {seperator}: required
    {dataType}: optional
    {Seperator}: optional
    {Value}: optional
    {seperator}: optional
    {end}: optional

    Custom binary format:
    {8bytes} : length of the entire message
    {1byte}: operation response code
    {2bytes}: length of key, 65536 characters are enough for key
    {n bytes}: n bytes as mentioned by previous value
    {2byte}: data type of value if value is present
    {4bytes}: length of the data, 2^32-1 is big enough for value
    {n bytes}: n bytes as mentioned by previous value
